("note","IMPORTANT","Common mistakes: *a hour, a honest boy* → **an hour, an honest boy**. *He is an university student* → **a university student**. *The Mount Everest, the Delhi, the India* → **Mount Everest, Delhi, India** (but **the Himalayas**). *I have a knowledge of the subject* → **knowledge**. *She is the M.A.* → **an M.A.** *He plays the cricket* → **cricket**. *The honesty is a virtue* → **Honesty is a virtue.**"),
("h2","4.3 Demonstrative Determiners"),
("table",["","Near","Far"],[["Singular","this book","that book"],["Plural","these books","those books"]]),
("ul",["*This / these* = close to the speaker in place or time (*this week, these days*); *that / those* = farther away (*that day, those years*).","Agree in number: *This book* (not *this books*); *those pencils*.","'Kind of / sort of / type of': *this kind of book*, *these kinds of books*; not *these kind of books* in careful English."]),
("h2","4.4 Possessive Determiners"),
("p","*My, our, your, his, her, its, their* come before a noun. They are never used together with an article: not *the my book*. For body parts and clothes the possessive is normal: *She raised **her** hand.* A noun in the possessive case also acts as a determiner: *Ravi's bag, the teacher's desk.*"),
("h2","4.5 Quantifiers: Number and Quantity Words"),
("table",["Determiner","With countable (plural) nouns","With uncountable nouns","Remark"],[
["some","✔ some books","✔ some water","In positive sentences and in offers/requests: *Would you like some tea?*"],
["any","✔ any books","✔ any water","In negatives and questions; in positive means 'no matter which': *Take any book.*"],
["much","✘","✔ much time","Mostly negatives/questions: *There isn't much milk.* Positive: use 'a lot of'."],
["many","✔ many friends","✘","*How many?* Positive: *many* is formal; 'a lot of' is common."],
["a lot of / lots of","✔","✔","Positive sentences, informal."],
["all","✔ all the boys","✔ all the milk","*All of them; all day.*"],
["both","✔ both hands","✘","Only two. *Both (of) the boys.*"],
["each","✔ (singular noun) each boy","✘","Takes singular verb: *Each student has a card.*"],
["every","✔ (singular) every child","✘","*Every one of them is ready.* Every + 'day' (all days); 'everyday' is an adjective."],
["either / neither","✔ (singular)","✘","Two things: *Either road is safe. Neither answer is right.*"],
["several","✔ several people","✘","More than two but not many."],
["enough","✔ enough chairs","✔ enough sugar","Before the noun; after adjectives/adverbs: *tall enough*."],
["more / most","✔","✔","*more books; most students*."],
["less / least","✘ (use fewer)","✔ less sugar","'Fewer' for countable; 'less' for uncountable: *fewer mistakes, less noise*."],
["another / other","✔ another book (singular); other books","✘","*another* = one more; *the other* = the remaining one."],
["no","✔ no problems","✔ no time","Before nouns; 'none' stands alone."]]),
("h3","Little, a little, the little"),
